 ```
 
+#### `window-focus-flash`
+
+A brief tint inside the focused window, fading to transparent.
+Automatic flashing is disabled by default; enable it with `on-focus`.
+The `color` alpha sets the highlight strength, and the usual animation timing settings apply.
+The highlight follows the window geometry and rounded corners, and stays below its popups.
+It also works with the focus ring disabled and with fullscreen windows.
+
+```kdl
+animations {
+    window-focus-flash {
+        on-focus
+        color "#ffffff26"
+        duration-ms 180
+        curve "ease-out-cubic"
+    }
+}
+binds {
+    Mod+Z { flash-window; }
+}
+```
+
+The `flash-window` action (also `niri msg action flash-window`) works independently of `on-focus`.
+Repeating it restarts the fade; losing keyboard focus cancels the highlight.
+Returning from a launcher or overview counts as gaining focus.
+Both `animations { off; }` and `window-focus-flash { off; }` disable manual and automatic flashes.
+Use `on-focus false` to disable only automatic flashes, including when overriding an included configuration.
+
 #### `window-close`
 
